00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.910 align:start position:0%
 
entrepreneurs like elon musk know  something about business that keeps them  ahead of the competition let's go  through his three-step formula by  analyzing tesla and spacex a little  later on we'll actually read some  internal company emails because elon  does some pretty interesting things  inside his businesses but first we need  to talk about something that's often  overlooked which takes us to step number  one elon has a system for getting  businesses off the ground what i've  noticed about some of the best  entrepreneurs in the world is that they  are incredible at identifying big  opportunities someone like elon is  constantly thinking of ideas his real  skill is being able to filter through  them and pick the one that has the best  chance of getting funding and attracting  talent and the good news is that there's  a bit of a system to this i've noticed  that the businesses that elon  prioritizes have to pass four main  criteria before he starts them the first  thing is all of elon's businesses have a  large addressable market it shouldn't be  a surprise that the biggest companies  tend to operate in the biggest markets  small markets are great for building  lifestyle businesses but elon wants more  the global car market is worth nearly  four trillion dollars so it's no  surprise that there are 40 car companies  worth more than 1 billion dollars the  second thing is that elon's companies  tend to operate in blue ocean markets  even though there are dozens of large  car companies there weren't any  manufacturers really taking electric  cars seriously when he started working  on tesla it's easy to attract talent and  capital when you're the only company  working on a new technology the same  thing is true for spacex reusable  rockets were heavily doubted for years  before elon and his team got them to  work but by taking a unique approach  from day one he basically had no real  competition who is your competition we  have no serious competition elon's  companies also build on his previous  skills in college he studied economics  and physics so when he built paypal he  was well equipped to understand the  economic problems in front of him then  when he started spacex he had no  experience in the aerospace industry but  he had managed a team of engineers  before and could leverage his physics  knowledge finally elon always stresses  the importance of building a world-class  team we'll cover some of the recruiting  tactics elon uses later in the video if  you look at any of elon's companies they  all follow these four criteria but now  it's time for the really interesting  parts because ideas are useless without  execution which takes us on to step  number two elon builds for exponential  growth i heard something about elon  recently that really surprised me and  it's one of the main reasons i wanted to  make this video in the first place  despite being worth over 200 billion  dollars elon still has a regular 10 pm  meeting on raptor engine design at  spacex now i've worked with plenty of  billion dollar company founders and  trust me this is very rare so why does  elon do this to himself well let's take  a listen to elon explaining why he is so  dedicated to spacex when you had that  third failure in a row  did you think  i need to pack this in never  why not  i don't ever give up  i'd have to be  dead or completely incapacitated okay so  elon's really hyped up his ability to  consistently raise the stakes financial  markets as we've discussed many times  before reward companies who can  consistently outperform expectations so  let's take a look at the number of  vehicles tesla was able to deliver over  the past 10 years  as you can see the growth in tesla  deliveries is almost perfectly  exponential but this wasn't just luck  elon had a strategy to deliver better  and better results each year he outlined  this in his secret plan back in 2006 the  goal was simple tesla would build a  high-end sports car to fund the  development of a sporty four-door family  car which in turn would fund an even  cheaper third model exponential growth  is all about timing elon focuses on the  product first the team will iterate on  the core design until it's ready to  produce then there's a big marketing  announcement that generates a wave of  hype he then channels all this hype into  pre-orders for the new vehicle this  helps generate cash for the business but  also validates demand and justifies  additional investment finally when the  cash is in the bank tesla can break  ground on a new manufacturing facility  to ramp up production building new  manufacturing capacity is extremely  risky but elon succeeds by using a  proven structure product customer demand  investment many companies fail because  they get this order wrong they raise too  much money too soon or they try to scale  a product that doesn't have proven  demand if you look a bit closer at the  tesla data you'll notice that model s  deliveries actually plateaued pretty  early on elon was already thinking ahead  though and had a plan to continue the  exponential growth technology innovation  usually follows an s-curve when a new  product like the tesla model s comes  along it takes off very quickly but then  it reaches maturity then a new  innovation window opens and a new  product can take off if it's better elon  is able to look into the future and  anticipate what technologies will  disrupt tesla and then start building  those technologies before the  competition can take over after the  model s proved that electric cars could  become popular he had to follow up with  a cheaper option in order to hit that  next part of the exponential curve and  elon followed this same strategy at  spacex and carefully staged investments  based on successful tests it took three  years for spacex to launch their first  falcon 1 rocket and it exploded after  just 33 seconds of flight progress was  slow at first and the second launch  didn't happen until 2007 but elon kept  pushing things forward at each stage the  team learned valuable lessons and  improved their technology that  eventually led spacex to win a massive  contract from nasa to deliver supplies  to the international space station over  the past 10 years spacex has steadily  increased capacity every year and is now  experiencing the exponential growth that  elon planned out when the company  started growing extremely quickly  creates lots of problems though as tesla  fought to double the amount of cars they  delivered each year it's easy to forget  about what was going on inside the  company to make that happen as a company  scales offices will get bigger more  people will get hired and everything  gets more complex that's why elon  insists that tesla employees always work  in the actual tesla offices in an email  earlier this year elon said that  everyone at tesla is required to spend a  minimum of 40 hours a week in the office  his goal is to keep people in sync with  each other and consistently push for  better results in the early days of  tesla elon lived in the factory and  slept on the floor also he could  constantly be in tune with production  and identify any blockers to growth this  type of decisive management doesn't work  unless your team is fully aligned with  your mission but elon has made it clear  that he's not just working for a quick  buck his companies are the type of place  where you can spend your entire career  and always be working on something new  to really build a massive company you  need to set yourself up for exponential  growth but for elon's formula there's  still a vital part that's missing which  takes us on to the next step elon  maximizes terminal value elon knows that  all his effort up to this point would be  useless if he doesn't capture as much of  the market as possible after all  exponential growth always comes to an  end when we see an exponential curve in  the real world we are actually seeing  just the beginning of a logistic curve  at some point the growth rate will start  to decline and eventually plateau you  can't just project out tesla deliveries  exponentially forever if you did you'd  eventually end up estimating that tesla  would sell more cars every year than  human beings on the planet which is just  impossible but elon recognizes that  hyper growth will inevitably end and he  plans for this first by operating in  only the largest markets his growth  curves will naturally have very high end  points tesla might eventually plateau  but at least it will still be operating  in one of the largest industries in the  world elon doesn't stop there though he  consistently creates opportunities to  increase the size of the market he's  going after with tesla that means  building self-driving car technology and  eventually humanoid robots as well the  timelines on these projects are  constantly slipping but that actually  doesn't matter as much as people think  as long as these technologies eventually  become valuable tesla will be able to  capitalize on them the same is true for  spacex where elon realized that the  market for launching rockets just wasn't  big enough so he had to build starlink  the aerospace industry is clearly  extremely important but the entire  launch market is just 8 billion  so it wouldn't be easy for elon to reach  his goals by sticking exclusively to  launches but the market for internet  connectivity is much bigger globally  broadband internet is worth over one  trillion dollars so by expanding his  business into this new area elon has  been able to justify additional  investment in spacex and ultimately  reshape the aerospace industry in the  process the impact of starlink on elon's  plans really can't be underestimated so  if you want to understand how elon is  strategizing for the next decade of  space exploration you have to watch this  video about how spacex makes money next  thanks for watching

